<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-ATLETICO CRASH 4-1 AT OVIEDO.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ATLETICO CRASH 4-1 AT OVIEDO.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atletico Madrid saw their chances of clinching Spain's second Champions' League place for next season all but disappear on Saturday when they lost 4-1 at Oviedo.</p>
<p>Ivan Iglesias and Oli Alvarez each scored twice to send Oviedo in at the break 4-0 up before Juan Esnaider pulled one back for the visitors.</p>
<p>Atletico stay five points behind fourth-placed Deportivo Coruna, and eight behind Betis and Barcelona, their main rivals for the second spot behind leaders Real Madrid.</p>
</text>
